{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Sally's Health and Wellness Column", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Writing About Health", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Organizing Points in an Argument", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use linking words to help you organize what you have written in a text.  It also helps you introduce and develop essential ideas.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Linking words help you to connect ideas and sentences, so that people can follow your ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here are some examples:<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>On the other hand</li><li>In fact</li><li>Of course</li><li>In addition</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In fact, the less time you have to plan meals and follow a regular exercise program, the more likely you are to become overwhelmed and exhausted. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In addition, there are many health blogs, websites that are written to provide information, tips and ideas.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Running in a cold climate is difficult for some people; on the other hand, it may improve the performance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Of course, your mom needs to know where you go.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Modals for Possibility and Certainty", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modals when you want to express possibility and certainty.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">You use <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to express possibility in the past and in the future.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "*<span class=\"italic\">Might </span>suggests that something is less possible than <span class=\"italic\">may</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">might </span>/ <span class=\"italic\">might not</span> + infinitive</li><li><span class=\"italic\">could </span>/ <span class=\"italic\">could not</span> + infinitive</li><li><span class=\"italic\">may </span>/ <span class=\"italic\">may not</span> + infinitive</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Expressing Certainty</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">must</span> to express that something is necessarily true", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">There are a number of things people must do to increase their longevity.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Others might find it challenge to fit in time for themselves within their work busy schedule. Hectic lifestyles encourage us make poor choices. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Some may perceive time outside the family as selfish and unwarranted.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to dedicate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to decide that something will be used for a special purpose", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you rarely dedicate time for exercise or regular medical check ups?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear in an article about health issues.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to perceive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to notice or become aware of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some may perceive time outside the family as selfish.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cardiovascular fitness", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the fitness of your heart", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to increase your cardiovascular fitness.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to monitor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to watch, observe, listen to, or check for a special purpose over a period of time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The doctor monitored the patient's vital signs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "dietary intake", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the food you consume", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your dietary intake should be looked at.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to take a toll", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cause damage or wear by hard living", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Too much stress can take a toll on anyone.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to carve out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to find time or space for something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Carve out some time for yourself.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob08aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a 120-150 word paragraph either agreeing or disagreeing with the following motion: <br/>The media has influenced people to consume unhealthy products. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use at least 3 linking words like <span class=\"italic\">In fact, ...</span> , and <span class=\"italic\">Also, ...</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use paragraph structure. Proofread your argument.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your argument aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What does your partner think of your argument? Is it convincing?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": " I write a text agreeing or disagreeing about health.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use linking words to connect ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my argument aloud to partner and ask for feedback.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can write about staying healthy.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can organize points in an argument.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express possibility and certainty.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you think you live a healthy lifestyle?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What do you think are ways to stay healthy? Exercise? Reducing stress? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedb